# Java Backend Development Research
1. What is Java?

Java is a high-level, object-oriented, class-based programming language.
It is widely used for enterprise applications, backend systems,
web applications, APIs, and distributed applications.

Java source code is compiled into bytecode, which runs on the Java
Virtual Machine (JVM).

## 2. JDK vs JRE vs JVM

### JVM

JVM stands for Java Virtual Machine. It executes Java bytecode and
provides platform independence.

### JRE

JRE stands for Java Runtime Environment. It provides the JVM and
libraries required to run Java applications.

### JDK

JDK stands for Java Development Kit. It contains the tools required
to develop Java applications, including the Java compiler and JRE.

Relationship:

JDK
 ├── Development tools
 └── JRE
      └── JVM

